      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T03:42:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not relying on assumption that either `DebianService` pr `forwarder`. `updateListeningPort` is working as producer of `UPDATE_EVT` and `UPDATE_QUEUE`, and `runForwarderHost` is working as the consumer of `UPDATE_EVT` and `UPDATE_QUEUE`. Regardless of the order between 2 function calls, it should work properly. Correct me if I\u0027m wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "728ec670_6aebc6d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "c4bccadd2e20074a95a0c2dc786d10a87938ae85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7bbad281_8f85aeff",
        "filename": "android/TerminalApp/java/com/android/virtualization/terminal/SettingsPortForwardingActivity.kt",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1386891
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T04:06:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "runForwarderHost can be notified by the event of UPDATE_EVT which is from updateListeningPort(which is called before runForwarderHost)?\n(I know the current flow `runForwarderHost` is always in prior to `updateListeningPort`, but I was worried about assumption)\n\nAnd also, it might be bad because we need to add `DebianServiceImpl.updateListeningPort` for everywhere port information can be manipulated. (Like this activity or by notification or maybe something triggered port listener).",
      "parentUuid": "f0a67a44_bfde9df9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "c4bccadd2e20074a95a0c2dc786d10a87938ae85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8943bbad_64e14f46",
        "filename": "android/TerminalApp/java/com/android/virtualization/terminal/SettingsPortForwardingActivity.kt",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T04:35:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e runForwarderHost can be notified by the event of UPDATE_EVT which is from updateListeningPort(which is called before runForwarderHost)?\n\nSince UPDATE_EVT is set as `LazyLock` with `static`, there\u0027s no correlation on the order of `runForwarderHost` and `updateListeningPort`. If `updateListeningPort` is called first, then `UPDATE_QUEUE` would have some data in it and it would be consumed when `runForwarderHost`. Vice versa, `runForwarderHost` will prepare for consuming with `poll_ctx.wait`, and consume right after `updateListeningPort` puts data into `UPDATE_QUEUE`.\n\n\u003e And also, it might be bad because we need to add DebianServiceImpl.updateListeningPort for everywhere port information can be manipulated.\n\nI can understand why it\u0027s bad. I thought it\u0027s a trivial thing. If the user manipulates port forwarding setting or listenable port is changed, shouldn\u0027t forwarder_host update its state?",
      "parentUuid": "7bbad281_8f85aeff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "c4bccadd2e20074a95a0c2dc786d10a87938ae85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
