      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T05:59:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Since UPDATE_EVT is set as LazyLock with static, there\u0027s no correlation on the order of runForwarderHost and updateListeningPort. If updateListeningPort is called first, then UPDATE_QUEUE would have some data in it and it would be consumed when runForwarderHost. Vice versa, runForwarderHost will prepare for consuming with poll_ctx.wait, and consume right after updateListeningPort puts data into UPDATE_QUEUE.\n\nAck.\n\n\u003e I can understand why it\u0027s bad. I thought it\u0027s a trivial thing. If the user manipulates port forwarding setting or listenable port is changed, shouldn\u0027t forwarder_host update its state?\n\nyeah, forwarder_host should know that, but I think DebianService should watch SharedPreference and then call `updateListeningPort` in the Debian service instead of calling `updateListeningPort` directly in several places.",
      "parentUuid": "8943bbad_64e14f46",
